// HZM coop - MP TAUNT wrappers so campaign AI can jeer at the players (2026-07-17, REBUILT 2026-07-18).
//
// bug-775: the original build copied the retail MP taunt alias lines (GRden_r_10..20 / AMdfr_r_10..20,
// the "Is that all you've got?" set). Those retail aliases are GHOST SUBTITLES - the WAV files were
// DELETED from the shipped paks (verified: zipfile scan of main/mainta/maintt pk3s finds none of them),
// so every taunt playsound resolved an alias whose audio does not exist -> silence, no console error.
// Retail MP had the same bug: those taunt voice commands never played in AA either.
//
// What DOES survive on disk (verified present, mono 22k, 0.7-3.0s each):
//   GRden_r_14/17/18/21  (5 voices a,b,c,d,i) - taunt-series lines, exact wording not in any alias
//                        table (the shipped audio kept only the numbers the retail aliases skipped),
//                        so these carry NO subtitle until someone ear-checks them.
//   AMdfr_r_14/17/18/21  (4 voices a,h,j,z)   - same deal, allied side.
//   GRden_v_* / AMdfr_v_* victory jeers with KNOWN retail subtitles ("Victory is ours!",
//                        "Your parents would be proud." etc). v_05 wording unknown (never aliased).
//
// de = German enemy taunts (coop_taunt_de1..33), us = US friendly taunts (coop_taunt_us1..29).
// Rolled by coop_mod/flchatter.scr, played positionally on a living AI. Parms mirror
// ubersound/coop_flvo.scr (the confirmed-working battle-chatter wrappers).
alias coop_taunt_de1 sound/dialogue/Multiplayer/g/GRden_r_14a.wav soundparms 1.0 0.1 1.0 0.05 320 2600 auto loaded maps "m e t dm obj train"
alias coop_taunt_de2 sound/dialogue/Multiplayer/g/GRden_r_14b.wav soundparms 1.0 0.1 1.0 0.05 320 2600 auto loaded maps "m e t dm obj train"
